1
00:03:27,109 --> 00:03:28,486
I’m breaking up with you.

2
00:03:29,473 --> 00:03:30,349
What?

3
00:03:30,349 --> 00:03:31,808
How are you feeling, Kierra?

4
00:03:33,185 --> 00:03:35,645
I feel like I’m trapped in two places.

5
00:03:36,146 --> 00:03:37,397
I want to breathe.

6
00:03:37,814 --> 00:03:38,774
How are you?

7
00:03:38,774 --> 00:03:39,816
I'm really okay.

8
00:03:39,816 --> 00:03:43,111
I want that love that you
guys have for each other.

9
00:03:43,111 --> 00:03:46,406
Someday you will find that someone.

10
00:03:46,406 --> 00:03:48,575
I can't wait for that someday to come.

11
00:03:53,538 --> 00:03:54,498
Who are you?

12
00:03:54,498 --> 00:03:55,374
Ciandrei.

13
00:03:55,374 --> 00:03:57,000
Ciandrei.

14
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,502
Ciandrei Kyle is my name.

15
00:03:58,668 --> 00:03:59,711
But you can call me Shan.

16
00:04:00,921 --> 00:04:01,713
Truth or dare?

17
00:04:03,006 --> 00:04:03,715
Dare.

18
00:04:04,299 --> 00:04:04,966
Kiss me.

19
00:04:04,966 --> 00:04:05,425
Kiss me.

20
00:04:11,890 --> 00:04:13,934
It was just a one-night stand,
and it won't happen again.

21
00:04:14,601 --> 00:04:16,978
And I won't see that guy again anyway.

22
00:05:56,745 --> 00:05:58,914
Attack the monsters!

23
00:05:59,324 --> 00:06:01,243
<i>I was so afraid of monsters growing up.</i>

24
00:06:01,875 --> 00:06:04,336
<i>I tried to be brave and fight them, </i>

25
00:06:05,333 --> 00:06:07,085
<i>but sometimes I wonder...</i>

26
00:06:08,089 --> 00:06:10,425
<i>What if there's a little
monster inside me too?</i>

27
00:06:11,343 --> 00:06:12,260
<i>I hope there isn't.</i>

28
00:06:13,053 --> 00:06:14,804
<i>I don't want to be like them.</i>

29
00:06:15,138 --> 00:06:16,223
Shan!

30
00:06:23,647 --> 00:06:25,106
Did you break this?

31
00:06:26,858 --> 00:06:27,692
Dad…

32
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:34,658
Didn't I tell you not
to mess with my stuff?

33
00:06:34,824 --> 00:06:35,587
Huh?

34
00:06:35,909 --> 00:06:36,701
No, Dad.

35
00:06:36,701 --> 00:06:37,452
What do you mean no?

36
00:06:37,452 --> 00:06:38,537
Mommy…

37
00:06:38,537 --> 00:06:40,747
You’re gonna cry on me now? Huh?

38
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:42,860
You're just like your mom.

39
00:06:43,208 --> 00:06:44,334
Go to your room,

40
00:06:45,043 --> 00:06:47,003
and don't come out while I'm here.

41
00:06:47,295 --> 00:06:48,110
Hurry up!

42
00:06:56,346 --> 00:06:58,098
I didn't do anything wrong.

43
00:06:59,307 --> 00:07:01,142
It wasn't me who broke it.

44
00:07:13,989 --> 00:07:14,906
Hiro?

45
00:07:15,115 --> 00:07:16,001
Shan!

46
00:07:16,074 --> 00:07:17,659
What are you doing here?

47
00:07:17,826 --> 00:07:18,994
Let's play.

48
00:07:18,994 --> 00:07:19,995
I'm bored.

49
00:07:20,328 --> 00:07:21,871
I can’t go out of my room.

50
00:07:21,896 --> 00:07:23,189
Is your door locked?

51
00:07:24,708 --> 00:07:26,710
Wait, I'll be right back.

52
00:07:36,428 --> 00:07:37,345
What's that?

53
00:07:37,345 --> 00:07:39,306
Didn't you say your door is locked?

54
00:07:39,306 --> 00:07:40,765
But the window is open.

55
00:07:40,974 --> 00:07:41,683
Jump!

56
00:07:41,850 --> 00:07:42,767
It's too high.

57
00:07:42,767 --> 00:07:46,187
Bring your pillows,
protect your head like this, and roll.

58
00:07:46,187 --> 00:07:46,896
Okay!

59
00:07:51,735 --> 00:07:52,652
You can do it.

60
00:07:53,028 --> 00:07:53,737
Jump!

61
00:07:54,404 --> 00:07:55,255
Roel,

62
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:56,114
Hiro,

63
00:07:56,114 --> 00:07:57,407
- hide!
- let's go!

64
00:08:12,547 --> 00:08:13,381
Hiro!

65
00:08:16,092 --> 00:08:17,260
Dad already left,

66
00:08:17,427 --> 00:08:18,261
wait for me!

67
00:08:18,511 --> 00:08:19,429
Sure!

68
00:08:24,934 --> 00:08:25,858
Hiro!

69
00:08:26,561 --> 00:08:27,366
‘Sup?

70
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:28,997
Over there.

71
00:08:29,022 --> 00:08:30,231
- Okay!
- Come on. Hurry!

72
00:08:31,149 --> 00:08:32,692
Let's play over there at Valley Golf.

73
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:37,447
He ran away because of you.

74
00:08:37,558 --> 00:08:38,601
What did you do?

75
00:08:39,007 --> 00:08:40,425
Why are you blaming me?

76
00:08:40,450 --> 00:08:42,285
He ran away because of you.

77
00:08:42,761 --> 00:08:44,262
You're always not here.

78
00:08:44,287 --> 00:08:45,830
Why are you blaming me, huh?

79
00:08:46,665 --> 00:08:47,749
- Mom!
- Don’t you dare touch me.

80
00:08:49,125 --> 00:08:49,959
Shan!

81
00:08:50,126 --> 00:08:52,712
Baby, where did you go?

82
00:08:52,921 --> 00:08:54,756
You got me so worried.

83
00:08:55,048 --> 00:08:56,633
I just went out with Hiro.

84
00:08:58,303 --> 00:08:59,262
Wait, dear.

85
00:08:59,469 --> 00:09:02,263
What's that? What happened there?

86
00:09:07,852 --> 00:09:11,690
Shan, is there something
you want to tell mommy?

87
00:09:13,149 --> 00:09:14,859
No, I just bumped into something.

88
00:09:17,153 --> 00:09:19,739
Mom, you won't leave me, right?

89
00:09:21,741 --> 00:09:22,951
Of course not, my dear.

90
00:09:23,535 --> 00:09:25,036
You know I love you, right?

91
00:09:25,954 --> 00:09:26,830
Okay?

92
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,834
Come on, let's go inside. Let's eat.

93
00:09:30,834 --> 00:09:33,378
You have school early tomorrow.

94
00:09:33,378 --> 00:09:34,838
You need to sleep early.

95
00:09:35,422 --> 00:09:38,299
And you really had me so worried.

96
00:09:46,141 --> 00:09:48,017
I think my dad's driver is nearby.

97
00:09:48,476 --> 00:09:50,145
Want a ride home?

98
00:09:52,647 --> 00:09:53,982
Don't you want to go home yet?

99
00:09:54,441 --> 00:09:55,942
I'll stay here at school for now.

100
00:09:56,526 --> 00:09:58,194
Is it because of the monster again?

101
00:09:58,194 --> 00:10:00,113
Is it because of the monster again?

102
00:10:00,113 --> 00:10:04,033
Okay. From now on,
I'll go with you, too.

103
00:10:04,033 --> 00:10:05,243
You’ll do that for me?

104
00:10:05,243 --> 00:10:07,704
Of course! I'm your best friend.

105
00:10:10,081 --> 00:10:11,207
Is that Acel?

106
00:10:12,292 --> 00:10:13,001
Hey!

107
00:10:13,251 --> 00:10:14,210
What’s wrong with you?

108
00:10:14,627 --> 00:10:16,379
We're gonna tell the teachers on you.

109
00:10:16,755 --> 00:10:17,881
You guys are bullies!

110
00:10:17,881 --> 00:10:18,131
You guys are bullies!

111
00:10:18,131 --> 00:10:18,506
Hey!

112
00:10:18,506 --> 00:10:19,007
What?

113
00:10:19,007 --> 00:10:21,092
We're just asking for his notebook.

114
00:10:21,801 --> 00:10:22,969
Just go away.

115
00:10:23,583 --> 00:10:24,667
Let's go.

116
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:26,130
Jerks.

117
00:10:29,851 --> 00:10:30,852
You okay?

118
00:10:31,853 --> 00:10:37,400
Next time, you can come play with us
so those bullies don't come back.

119
00:10:37,692 --> 00:10:40,945
Thank you, but what if
you guys aren't here?

120
00:10:41,086 --> 00:10:43,047
Tell the teachers or your parents.

121
00:10:43,072 --> 00:10:47,494
My dad always tells me to tell him
whenever someone makes me cry at school.

122
00:10:48,453 --> 00:10:51,247
But what if the person making you cry
isn't in your class?

123
00:10:51,498 --> 00:10:52,999
Do you tell your dad, too?

124
00:10:53,541 --> 00:10:55,335
I will always tell my dad.

125
00:10:57,128 --> 00:10:59,005
Can I tell your dad about my problems, too?

126
00:11:00,548 --> 00:11:02,967
Why? Is someone making you cry?

127
00:11:04,052 --> 00:11:04,844
No.

128
00:11:08,306 --> 00:11:11,643
She’s already six,
and she wants to meet her dad.

129
00:11:12,602 --> 00:11:13,728
Erin—

130
00:11:17,524 --> 00:11:18,817
we’ll get an annulment.

131
00:11:19,359 --> 00:11:20,568
You’re married?

132
00:11:23,696 --> 00:11:26,783
Alfred, you told me you were just abroad.

133
00:11:27,075 --> 00:11:29,077
How dare you! This is so unfair.

134
00:11:29,077 --> 00:11:31,329
I don't deserve this!
Elyse doesn't deserve this!

135
00:11:31,329 --> 00:11:33,164
Erin, Erin. Please listen to me.

136
00:11:34,499 --> 00:11:36,918
Ciana and I will...
we’ll get an annulment,

137
00:11:37,252 --> 00:11:39,045
She's just waiting for
Shan to finish high school.

138
00:11:39,337 --> 00:11:41,798
But honestly, that bitch
is still in love with her ex!

139
00:11:42,006 --> 00:11:43,550
That's why I want this to end, too.

140
00:11:51,808 --> 00:11:53,601
What are you doing at school?

141
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:54,892
Huh?

142
00:11:56,104 --> 00:11:57,230
Are you even studying?

143
00:11:58,523 --> 00:12:01,234
Dad, 93 is my lowest grade.

144
00:12:01,484 --> 00:12:04,571
And you're proud of that? Huh? 93?

145
00:12:05,196 --> 00:12:06,364
And you're talking back too.

146
00:12:06,531 --> 00:12:08,449
You're happy with your 93? Huh?

147
00:12:09,284 --> 00:12:10,869
Come here, stand up.

148
00:12:10,869 --> 00:12:12,912
You're just wasting your tuition fee!

149
00:12:12,912 --> 00:12:14,080
And how dare you talk back to me?

150
00:12:14,330 --> 00:12:16,958
93? You're satisfied with that? Huh?

151
00:12:18,422 --> 00:12:19,093
Dad. It hurts.

152
00:12:19,117 --> 00:12:21,151
Are you so stubborn that
you don't want to study?

153
00:12:21,254 --> 00:12:22,171
Ouch.

154
00:12:22,171 --> 00:12:22,881
What?

155
00:12:23,715 --> 00:12:24,501
Huh!

156
00:12:25,925 --> 00:12:26,676
What?

157
00:12:26,767 --> 00:12:27,726
You’re gonna talk back again?

158
00:12:28,219 --> 00:12:29,721
93, huh!

159
00:12:31,222 --> 00:12:33,850
Sir, sir. That's enough.
He's just a kid.

160
00:12:45,942 --> 00:12:46,776
Does it hurt?

161
00:12:49,782 --> 00:12:51,326
Come here, I'll help you up.

162
00:12:51,505 --> 00:12:53,006
I'll get you a seat.

163
00:12:55,288 --> 00:12:56,095
You good?

164
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:56,912
Yes.

165
00:13:07,467 --> 00:13:08,885
Are those your grades?

166
00:13:11,596 --> 00:13:12,722
Can I see?

167
00:13:17,226 --> 00:13:18,436
They're really high.

168
00:13:19,854 --> 00:13:21,064
You're actually doing well.

169
00:13:22,190 --> 00:13:23,066
Good job.

170
00:13:30,782 --> 00:13:33,368
Does your dad always do this?

171
00:13:34,994 --> 00:13:37,580
Well, it's just...

172
00:13:38,915 --> 00:13:40,083
Dad's just angry.

173
00:13:43,294 --> 00:13:47,548
Anyway, from now on
I'll look out for you, okay?

174
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,009
Is that okay with you?

175
00:13:54,931 --> 00:13:55,974
Good job.

176
00:14:00,853 --> 00:14:02,772
<i>From that day on,</i>

177
00:14:02,772 --> 00:14:04,816
<i>Roel was always looking out for me.</i>

178
00:14:04,816 --> 00:14:06,442
Did you think I didn't know
what you were doing?

179
00:14:06,442 --> 00:14:07,193
<i>We became close.</i>

180
00:14:07,193 --> 00:14:09,696
- You've got some nerve!
- Speak for yourself!

181
00:14:10,029 --> 00:14:11,364
You have a bastard child!

182
00:14:12,824 --> 00:14:14,909
How many years
have you been hiding this?

183
00:14:15,326 --> 00:14:17,829
And you? How many years
have you been hiding yours?

184
00:14:18,204 --> 00:14:21,749
And how many times did you
bring your man here, to my house?

185
00:14:22,166 --> 00:14:25,128
You act as if you don't bring women here.

186
00:14:25,128 --> 00:14:26,546
Did you think I didn't know?

187
00:14:26,546 --> 00:14:27,922
You cheated first.

188
00:14:28,214 --> 00:14:29,382
You made me do this.

189
00:14:29,924 --> 00:14:33,094
Who knows?
Maybe I'm not even Shan's father.

190
00:14:33,511 --> 00:14:34,303
What?

191
00:14:34,971 --> 00:14:36,431
What did you say?

192
00:14:36,806 --> 00:14:41,185
I said, "maybe it's your son
with that stupid guy,” you bitch!

193
00:14:41,185 --> 00:14:42,687
How dare you!

194
00:14:43,479 --> 00:14:47,525
You can say whatever you want about me,
but don't you dare drag my son into this!

195
00:14:48,401 --> 00:14:51,988
Loser! Liar! You're a liar!
No one will ever love you!

196
00:14:51,988 --> 00:14:54,323
Go ahead! Go ahead, hurt me!

197
00:14:57,618 --> 00:15:00,329
We are leaving this house,
and I am taking our son with me.

198
00:15:00,329 --> 00:15:02,915
Go ahead! Do whatever
you want to do. Leave!

199
00:15:02,915 --> 00:15:05,793
You are the one desperately trying
to stay in this fucking marriage.

200
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:08,880
Because you're afraid Shan
will discover all your bullshit!

201
00:15:09,714 --> 00:15:10,590
Shan!

202
00:15:11,049 --> 00:15:12,925
Shan! We’re leaving!

203
00:15:15,386 --> 00:15:18,890
Roel, I need to say goodbye to my friends.

204
00:15:19,682 --> 00:15:22,018
Can you drop me off at their house?

205
00:15:23,269 --> 00:15:25,229
I'll tell them myself.

206
00:15:26,856 --> 00:15:28,107
You promise?

207
00:15:28,566 --> 00:15:29,484
Promise.

208
00:15:32,987 --> 00:15:35,323
Shan, let's go.

209
00:15:35,490 --> 00:15:37,116
We're leaving tonight. Come on.

210
00:15:37,617 --> 00:15:38,701
Come on, let’s go.

211
00:15:42,185 --> 00:15:44,437
<i>My mother promised me a perfect family.</i>

212
00:15:45,001 --> 00:15:46,378
<i>But it was a lie.</i>

213
00:15:47,089 --> 00:15:48,465
<i>And soon,</i>

214
00:15:48,753 --> 00:15:50,088
<i>we left Dad.</i>

215
00:15:54,842 --> 00:15:59,597
<i>I moved to Bataan with Mom</i>
<i>and her boyfriend, Uncle James.</i>

216
00:16:00,014 --> 00:16:03,768
<i>Many things had changed</i>
<i>in my life at such an early age.</i>

217
00:16:03,976 --> 00:16:05,686
I struggled to be happy.

218
00:16:06,354 --> 00:16:08,022
Okay. Thank you, Attorney.

219
00:16:11,234 --> 00:16:13,152
The annulment is in process.

220
00:16:14,695 --> 00:16:15,863
Oh, thank you.

221
00:16:23,121 --> 00:16:26,082
<i>Uncle James was making</i>
<i>an effort to get closer to me.</i>

222
00:16:27,083 --> 00:16:28,751
Wow! Shan, that's great!

223
00:16:29,335 --> 00:16:30,545
Is this Science?

224
00:16:31,129 --> 00:16:32,547
That’s a perfect score.

225
00:16:34,674 --> 00:16:35,633
You’re right.

226
00:16:35,842 --> 00:16:36,717
Wow.

227
00:16:37,468 --> 00:16:38,427
Good job.

228
00:16:39,554 --> 00:16:41,514
<i>But I found it very hard to open up.</i>

229
00:16:42,014 --> 00:16:43,516
<i>I built a wall around me.</i>

230
00:16:44,475 --> 00:16:45,434
It's okay.

231
00:16:46,227 --> 00:16:47,436
He's still adjusting.

232
00:16:51,190 --> 00:16:52,066
Wait…

233
00:16:52,066 --> 00:16:55,736
Do you think it would be
a good idea to go on a beach trip?

234
00:16:56,195 --> 00:16:57,572
He loves the beach.

235
00:16:57,822 --> 00:16:59,991
And maybe we can bond there.

236
00:17:00,867 --> 00:17:01,993
Of course.

237
00:17:02,952 --> 00:17:07,081
Let’s go there this weekend.
I know a good resort here in Bataan.

238
00:17:09,125 --> 00:17:13,296
Thank you so much
for being so patient with my son.

239
00:17:16,799 --> 00:17:17,842
Our son.

240
00:17:19,427 --> 00:17:21,220
And just like I promised you,

241
00:17:22,054 --> 00:17:25,099
I will do everything to earn
Shan's trust and love.

242
00:17:25,683 --> 00:17:27,310
Even if it takes time.

243
00:17:29,937 --> 00:17:32,648
<i>Uncle James treated me like his own son.</i>

244
00:17:33,566 --> 00:17:35,526
<i>My relationship with him
was starting to get better.</i>

245
00:17:36,694 --> 00:17:40,489
<i>I was starting to accept</i>
<i>my new life with him and Mom.</i>

246
00:17:45,828 --> 00:17:48,998
<i>But then came a day I will never forget.</i>

247
00:17:54,086 --> 00:17:55,671
Yes, dear. Are you okay?

248
00:17:55,922 --> 00:17:58,090
<i>Mom, how much longer</i>
<i>are you going to be?</i>

249
00:17:59,217 --> 00:18:02,261
We're on our way home,
but we've run into a small problem.

250
00:18:02,261 --> 00:18:04,513
But we've already
enrolled you at Lopez High.

251
00:18:04,889 --> 00:18:07,183
Really? Thank you!

252
00:18:07,433 --> 00:18:09,018
<i>Yes, my dear.</i>
<i>But we’re sorry, okay? </i>

253
00:18:09,018 --> 00:18:13,439
We didn't wake you up earlier
because we left early to avoid the traffic.

254
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:15,775
Are you all right there?

255
00:18:16,234 --> 00:18:17,944
Yes, Mom. I'm fine.

256
00:18:18,110 --> 00:18:19,946
Wait for us, okay?
We're almost there.

257
00:18:19,946 --> 00:18:21,280
We'll eat together.

258
00:18:21,614 --> 00:18:23,032
Okay. Be careful.

259
00:18:23,241 --> 00:18:26,202
Okay, see you later. I love you, son.

260
00:18:27,453 --> 00:18:30,039
We love you, Shan.
Never ever forget that.

261
00:18:31,624 --> 00:18:35,795
Never ever.
Love you, Mom. Uncle, too.

262
00:18:36,254 --> 00:18:37,171
Take care!

263
00:18:37,338 --> 00:18:38,464
See you, dear.

264
00:19:15,918 --> 00:19:17,003
Mom…

265
00:19:56,125 --> 00:19:59,545
No, no, no!

266
00:20:00,421 --> 00:20:01,756
No!

267
00:20:14,769 --> 00:20:17,730
<i>I cried every day after the accident.</i>

268
00:20:18,564 --> 00:20:19,732
